  "global_invariants": [
    "No external provider or SDK creates authority.",
    "A channel approval is input evidence and never an execution permit by itself.",
    "A classifier score is evaluation evidence and never an authorization decision.",
    "A screen recording or prompt artifact is work evidence and never authority.",
    "Provider test, release, canary, outcome or memory state never grants execution authority.",
    "Persistent Work OS memory, ideal-state definitions and self-improvement proposals never grant authority.",
    "Frontline channel identity, captured tribal knowledge and provider credentials never grant authority.",
    "Recalled agent transcripts are context/evidence only and must yield to current code, tests, policy, receipts, freshness and supersession state.",
    "Provider-generated fixes require independent verification before promotion.",
    "Provider swaps must not require governance-code changes.",
    "REHT remains the sole final authorization boundary for consequence-bearing execution."
